\chapter{Relativistic Propulsion Kernels in the Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE)}
\section{Overview}

The second chapter of the TSSE monograph formalizes the relativistic propulsion
kernel architecture. TSSE imposes strict temporal symmetry, phase-space invariance,
and symplectic evolution constraints on all admissible dynamical systems. When
applied to relativistic propulsion, these constraints yield a unique class of
Hamiltonian engines whose exhaust dynamics, energy transfer, and structural
manifold evolution obey TSSE invariants.

This chapter establishes:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item The relativistic Hamiltonian foundations of TSSE propulsion kernels.
  \item The temporal symmetry constraints on relativistic exhaust.
  \item The structural manifold invariants governing engine stability.
  \item The theorem--lemma--proof hierarchy defining admissible relativistic engines.
  \item The canonical TSSE Relativistic Propulsion Kernel (TSSE-RPK).
\end{enumerate}

