\section{Relativistic Hamiltonian Foundations}

Let the state of a propulsion system be represented by canonical coordinates
$(q,p)$ evolving under a relativistic Hamiltonian $H$ of the form:
\[
H(q,p) = \sqrt{m^2c^4 + c^2\|p\|^2} + V(q),
\]
where $V(q)$ encodes structural, magnetic, and confinement potentials.

\subsection{TSSE-Admissibility Conditions}

A relativistic Hamiltonian $H$ is TSSE-admissible if:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item It commutes with the temporal symmetry operator:
  \[
  [H,\mathcal{T}] = 0.
  \]
  \item It generates a symplectic flow:
  \[
  \mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J.
  \]
  \item It preserves the structural manifold $\mathcal{S}$:
  \[
  \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S} = \mathcal{S}.
  \]
\end{enumerate}

These conditions define the admissible class of relativistic TSSE propulsion kernels.

