\section{Temporal Symmetry Constraints on Relativistic Exhaust}

Let $v_e$ denote the exhaust velocity of the propulsion system. TSSE requires:
\[
\mathcal{T}v_e = -v_e,
\]
ensuring that the exhaust dynamics are consistent with time-reversal symmetry.

\begin{lemma}[Temporal Reversal of Exhaust]
If $[H,\mathcal{T}] = 0$, then the exhaust velocity satisfies:
\[
v_e(t) = -v_e(-t).
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{T}$ commutes with $H$, the evolution operator satisfies:
\[
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(-t)\mathcal{T}.
\]
Applying this to the exhaust momentum $p_e$ yields:
\[
p_e(t) = -p_e(-t),
\]
and dividing by relativistic mass gives the stated result.
\end{proof}

This lemma ensures that TSSE engines preserve temporal symmetry even under relativistic exhaust conditions.

