\section{Canonical TSSE Relativistic Propulsion Kernel (TSSE-RPK)}

The TSSE-RPK is defined by the tuple:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-RPK}} =
\left(
H,\;
\mathcal{T},\;
\mathcal{S},\;
\mathcal{U}(t)
\right),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $H$ is a relativistic TSSE-admissible Hamiltonian.
  \item $\mathcal{T}$ is the temporal symmetry operator.
  \item $\mathcal{S}$ is the structural manifold.
  \item $\mathcal{U}(t)$ is the symplectic evolution operator.
\end{itemize}

The kernel enforces:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J,
\qquad
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{T},
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S} = \mathcal{S}.
\]

This kernel forms the mathematical backbone of all TSSE-governed relativistic engines,
including the AITFE architecture.

